 "tier1Summary": "A week after their midterm defeat, Republicans are regrouping: Trump made [[p:Stephen Miller (political advisor)|Stephen Miller]] chief of staff, [[p:Jim Jordan]] will lead House Republicans, and the House shelved an Iran-war impeachment of [[p:Pete Hegseth]]. Democrats lead both uncalled Senate races and eye the 11 Dec funding deadline to curb the war.\n\nCanada reports softer US demands; Canada and Mexico both meet Xi at APEC. [[p:María Corina Machado]] backed Washington's Venezuela roadmap, new sanctions hit Chinese suppliers of Cuba, ousted Paraguayan president [[p:Santiago Peña]] is in detention, and Salvadoran troops struck a major Haitian gang.\n\nElsewhere, the Abu Dhabi talks ended with a prisoner-swap deal but no breakthrough, Merz is tying the EU budget to Ukraine funding, and Iran denies talks as tankers burn in Hormuz.",
